        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fde28989-bfb7-5b47-bef6-b03d05ee8389",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dean Jones, Laurens van der Post\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Works: The Million Dollar Duck, The $1,000,000 Duck, A Far Off Place, A Far-Off Place, A Story Like the Wind, The Love Bug, Beethoven\n- Topics: American comedy films, adventure drama films, golden eggs, film adaptations, Golden Globe nominations\n\nFacts:\n- Walt Disney Productions produced The Million Dollar Duck, also titled The $1,000,000 Duck, as a 1971 American comedy film about a goose that lays golden eggs.\n- Laurens van der Post wrote A Story Like the Wind in 1972 and A Far-Off Place in 1974.\n- Dean Jones played Jim Douglas in The Love Bug in 1968.\n- Dean Jones played Albert Dooley in The Million Dollar Duck in 1971 and received a Golden Globe nomination for that role.\n- Dean Jones played Dr. Herman Varnick in Beethoven in 1992.\n- A Far Off Place is a 1993 American adventure drama film based on Laurens van der Post's works A Far-Off Place and its prequel A Story Like the Wind.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d1697a04-9776-566c-9204-639b9dfc9950",
        "text": "Page: The Million Dollar Duck. Sentence: The Million Dollar Duck (also titled as The $1,000,000 Duck) is a 1971 American comedy film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a goose that lays golden eggs scenario.\nPage: A Far Off Place. Sentence: A Far Off Place is a 1993 American adventure drama film based on Laurens van der Post's works \"A Far-Off Place\" (1974) and its prequel \"A Story Like the Wind\" (1972).\nPage: Dean Jones (actor). Sentence: \" (1965), Jim Douglas in \"The Love Bug\" (1968), Albert Dooley in \"The Million Dollar Duck\" (1971; for which he received a Golden Globe nomination) and Dr. Herman Varnick in \"Beethoven\" (1992).",
